.TH CCOL_EVENT_LOOP_CONSTRUCT 3 "2026-07-12" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
ccol_event_loop_construct \- declare and initialise a ccol_event_loop in one step
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_event_loop_construct(name, max_events_per_wait, num_lock_stripes,
                     num_reactor_threads);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Declares a ccol_event_loop variable named name, calls ccol_event_loop_create() to
initialise it, and calls ccol_fatal_err() if creation fails.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
name                  Variable name for the ccol_event_loop handle.
max_events_per_wait   Size of the epoll_wait batch buffer the polling
                      thread uses (must be between 1 and INT_MAX
                      inclusive, and small enough that
                      max_events_per_wait * sizeof(struct epoll_event)
                      does not overflow size_t).
num_lock_stripes      Number of independent lock stripes for the fd/entry
                      registry (must be >= 1).  1 means a single
                      shared lock.
num_reactor_threads   Number of background reactor threads (must be
                      >= 1; 1 means a single thread that both polls
                      and dispatches inline).
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Calls ccol_fatal_err() on failure; use ccol_event_loop_create() or
ccol_event_loop_create_with_mprocs() directly when graceful error handling
is required.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ccol_event_loop_construct(loop, 32, 1, 1);
ccol_event_reg reg = ccol_event_loop_add(loop, ccol_selectable_from_fd(fd, ccol_select_read),
                                handlers, NULL, NULL);
ccol_event_loop_remove(loop, reg);
ccol_event_loop_destroy(loop);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_event_loop_construct_scoped (3),
.BR ccol_event_loop_declare (3),
.BR ccol_event_loop_create (3),
.BR ccol_event_loop_add (3),
.BR ccol_event_loop_destroy (3)
